## Exact sector action

In the fixed B103 order, write a state as

```text
v=(v_H20,v_H11,v_H02)
```

with dimensions `248+1013+248=1509`. G3CD emits three exact recursive source
blocks

```text
K_H20 : GF(11)^248  -> GF(11)^1509,
K_H11 : GF(11)^1013 -> GF(11)^1509,
K_H02 : GF(11)^248  -> GF(11)^1509.
```

The complete action is exactly

```text
K v = K_H20 v_H20 + K_H11 v_H11 + K_H02 v_H02.
```

For the homogeneous affine lift,

```text
K_tilde(v,s)=(K v+s b,0).
```

## Full-frame replay

The G3CM builder never loads the dense terminal operator. Starting with the
selected source `b`, it repeatedly applies only the three sparse sector maps.
All `1,509` resulting vectors agree entrywise with the G3CJ Krylov frame:

```text
[b,Kb,...,K^1508b].
```

The independently verified mismatch count is zero across all
`1509 x 1509` compared entries. The next action also satisfies the emitted
degree-1,509 G3CJ recurrence with zero residual.

A second verifier concatenates the three blocks and checks that every entry
equals the frozen dense G3CD operator before independently replaying the
sequence. Thus matrix-free and dense execution are not merely numerically
close; they are the same finite linear map.

## Family execution consequence

Every stage used to construct the sector blocks is linear: source formation,
toric return, original-Jacobian reduction, recursive divergence and chart
solve. Therefore, at a family point, one may combine the current coordinates
before executing the return machinery:

```text
H20 lane: combine 248 coefficients, then one -3 P sC return chain;
H11 lane: combine 1013 coefficients, then one -4 P sC return chain;
H02 lane: combine 248 coefficients, then one -5 P sC pole-six return chain.
```

One connection right-hand-side evaluation therefore needs three combined
sector chains, not materialization of 1,509 individual columns. The carrier
and state remain 1,509-dimensional; this is a matrix-free execution theorem,
not dimensional reduction.

